{:receipt/id "2026-08-23-bridge-materialize-scaling"
 :receipt/date "2026-08-23"
 :receipt/what "kotobase.query.bridge/materialize -- the path the DEPLOYED query surfaces (sparql/cypher/gremlin/graphql .kotobase.net) take -- measured against database size"
 :receipt/why "ADR-2607172300 accepted the linear scan as a v0.1 limitation and made revisiting it conditional on `real query-volume evidence`. ADR-2608039975 then measured that nobody was paying for it, because the six surface repos had no deploy shell. That is no longer the shape: kotobase-protocols-worker.query mounts four of them on live hostnames, and it composes them onto `kotobase.query.bridge`. Nobody had put a number on what that costs."
 :receipt/host-load "load average 169 during the run; 3 users, many concurrent agent sessions. ABSOLUTE MILLISECONDS ARE CONTAMINATED and are not to be quoted. What survives is the SHAPE across the four sizes, all taken inside one process within seconds of each other."
 :receipt/method "clojure -M on kotoba-lang/kotobase-query's own deps (kotobase bbf57df, arrangement a5d68dc). n documents in one collection, each {:rdfs/subClassOf ... :label ...}, put through kotobase.local/local-store. One warm call before each measured call. Query is a single-clause BGP over the materialized db."
 :receipt/measurements
 [{:documents 500   :materialize-ms 17.0  :query-ms 31.2 :datoms 500   :note "query-ms is JIT warm-up, not a result"}
  {:documents 2000  :materialize-ms 67.1  :query-ms 0.9  :datoms 2000}
  {:documents 8000  :materialize-ms 176.4 :query-ms 0.8  :datoms 8000}
  {:documents 32000 :materialize-ms 460.9 :query-ms 1.2  :datoms 32000}]
 :receipt/finding "materialize is linear in the DATABASE and the query is flat in the ANSWER: 4x the documents costs 3.9x/2.6x/2.6x more materialize, while the query stays near 1ms across a 64x range. So essentially the whole cost of a query on these surfaces is rebuilding a database value that the answer did not need -- the same 92%-hydration shape ADR-2607310900 measured on the OTHER live path, now measured here too."
 :receipt/lower-bound "This is an in-memory floor and not the live number. It excludes the R2/B2 block reads kotobase-protocols-worker pays to hydrate its LocalStore before materialize even starts. The live cost is strictly worse than this."
 :receipt/why-an-index-does-not-fix-it-here "Not a wiring gap. kotobase-protocols-worker stores DOCUMENTS as datoms -- entity (pr-str [:doc coll k]), attrs `doc/coll` / `doc/key` / `doc/val`, with the document's whole value as one EDN blob in `doc/val` (kotobase-protocols-worker.kotobase-store's own ns docstring). The triples a SPARQL query matches do not exist as datoms in that store; they exist inside the blobs. No predicate index can narrow a read for a triple that was never stored as one. Pointing this surface at kotobase.server.pattern-source is a DATA MODEL change, not a routing change, and this receipt exists so that is decided with the number in front of it."
